1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose
The AtmosAI weather app will be built using React JS and the Open Weather Map API. The
purpose of the application will be to allow the user to search for a location and see various
weather conditions in the area. These weather conditions will include temperature, humidity,
wind speed, weather descriptions, and forecast information. Amongst many more features, the
one that stands out is the AI summary implementation. An example of this feature would be
that if it is raining outside, the summary might say something like: “That rain is really coming
down outside! You’ll probably want an umbrella and some rain boots if you decide to venture
outside today!”
1.2 Document Conventions
This document follows the Software Requirements Specification (SRS) template of Karl Wiegers.
Section headings use hierarchical numbering to organize the requirements and also make specific
sections easy to reference. Unique requirement IDs are used to support traceability and show the
functional requirements. Requirements are written in a way that is very clear and specific. Each
feature has a priority level of high, medium, or low based on its importance and function.
Technical terms and abbreviations are defined when necessary so maintain clarity throughout the
document.
1.3 Intended Audience and Reading Suggestions
This SRS is intended for developers, testers, project members, and potential users of AtmosAI.
Developers should use this document to understand core features of this application and expected
behavior. Testers should use the functional and non-functional requirements to develop test cases
for the application. Project team members should use the document to understand the project’s
scope and development goals. Potential users can consult the introductory sections to understand
the purpose and capabilities of AtmosAI.
Readers should begin with the first 2 sections to understand the purpose, scope, and functionality
of the program. Section 3 describes the external interfaces and integrations required for the
application. Section 4 specifies the system’s features and functional requirements, and section 5
describes its non-functional requirements. The appendices provide supporting information
including analysis models.
1.4 Product Scope
AtmosAI is an AI-enhanced weather application that will provide users with
up-to-date weather information and personalized summaries of weather conditions
along with suggestions for the day. Users will be able to view current weather
conditions, forecasts, weather maps, check air quality information, and manage saved
locations. The goal of AtmosAI is to help users understand weather conditions more
easily and make informed decisions about their daily activities. By combining
traditional weather data with AI-generated explanations and recommendations, the
