2. Overall Description
2.1 Product Perspective
AtmosAI is a new and self-contained weather application developed as a software engineering
project. It is designed to combine traditional weather data with AI to help users understand weather
conditions and how these conditions should influence their daily activities. The application will use
a React-based web interface so that users can search for locations and view weather conditions and
forecasts. External sources will provide the primary weather data. OpenWeatherMap API will
supply weather data and forecasts, while OpenAI API will generate the weather summaries.
Atmos AI is not intended to replace existing weather data providers, but it is instead designed to
serve as an interface that combines weather data with AI-generated explanations. Its functionality
will depend on the availability and capabilities of the external APIs it uses
2.2 Product Functions
- Weather Information: Allow users to search for weather conditions by ZIP
code and view current conditions including temperature, humidity, wind,
precipitation probability, and a weather description. Provide a five-day
forecast and short-term forecasts hourly.
- AI-Powered Assistance: Generate daily weather summaries and suggested
actions with artificial intelligence to help users understand the weather.
- Location Management and Personalization: Allow users to save locations
and change measurement units according to their preferences.
- Environmental Information: Provide Air Quality Index (AQI) information
to help users understand local air quality.
- Weather Data Management: Cache weather information to improve
accessibility, display the time the data was retrieved, and update cached
weather data every two hours.
Software Requirements Specification for AtmosAI Page 5
2.3 User Classes and Characteristics
- General Weather App Users: This is the primary user class for AtmosAI. These users access the
application to check current weather conditions, view forecasts, and plan their days. This is the
most important one to satisfy as AtmosAI is primarily intended to provide convenient weather
information to the general public.
- Frequent Planners and Travelers: This user class includes people who rely on weather information
when planning trips, vacations, or work. Their needs emphasize convenient access to forecasts and
weather information in different places, but are overall very similar to the general user.
- Maintenance and Development Personnel: This class includes developers and maintainers
responsible for troubleshooting and updating AtmosAI. They rely on the SRS to understand
expected system behavior and maintain consistency as the application evolves.
2.4 Constraints
- Privacy and Data Handling: The application should limit the collection and storage of user data, but
of course save what is necessary such as preferences and locations.
- Hardware and Browser Compatibility: AtmosAI will operate as a web application and be usable on
desktop and mobile browsers. Performance will depend on the user’s device capabilities and internet
connection as well.
- External API Dependencies: The application relies on the OpenWeatherMap API for weather
information and the OpenAI API for AI-generated summaries and suggestions.
- Concurrent Use: The application should accommodate multiple users accessing weather data at the
same time without performance dips.
- Error Logging and Troubleshooting: Application and API errors should be identifiable so developers
can diagnose problems. The logs should not expose sensitive information.
- User Controls: The interface must provide access to the application’s supported controls such as
location, unit selection, and saved location management.
- Programming Technologies: The application is developed using React and JavaScript.
Implementation decisions must remain compatible with the project’s selected technologies and
architecture.
2.5 Operating Environment
AtmosAI is a web-based application developed using React and JavaScript. It is intended to
operate on desktop computers, laptops, and any device that has a modern web browser.
Supporting operating systems include Windows, macOS, Android, and iOS, depending on
browser compatibility.
The application requires internet connectivity to retrieve weather information from the APIs.
This means that it is externally reliant upon these services and the user’s network connection.
Cached information may be available during connection interruptions depending on the
application’s implementation. There will be no other application necessary besides a modern web
browser.
Software Requirements Specification for AtmosAI Page 6
2.6 Design and Implementation Constraints
- Development Technologies: The application uses React and JavaScript. New components and
features must remain compatible with the existing application framework.
- External API Integration: AtmosAI relies on the OpenWeatherMap API for weather data and the
OpenAI API for AI-generated summaries and suggested actions. Developers must follow the
API’s supported request formats and usage limits.
- Network Communication: Retrieving current weather information and generating AI responses
requires communication with external internet services. Network delays or service interruptions
may affect the application.
- Security and Credentials: API credentials must be handled securely and must not be exposed
through publicly accessible client-side code. Server components must also protect user
credentials.
- Performance Requirements: The application should retrieve and display weather data.
AI-generated content may also be affected by the external AI service.
- Data Storage: The caching and saved-location functionality must be compatible with the browser
environment.
- Development and Maintenance: Implementation decisions should remain consistent with the
team’s existing codebase and coding practices.
2.7 User Documentation
AtmosAI will include concise digital user documentation to help users understand how to search
for weather information. Basic troubleshooting guidance for common issues may be included as
well.
2.8 Assumptions and Dependencies
- Internet Connectivity: User’s personal network connections limit their access to the features
of the program.
- Weather Data Provider: AtmosAI depends on the OpenWeatherMap API to provide the
weather conditions and forecasts.
- AI Service Provider: AtmosAI depends on the OpenAI API to generate weather summaries
and suggested actions.
- API Credential and Usage Limits: The project assumes that valid credentials and sufficient
API usage allowances will be available throughout development and operation.
- Browser Support: Users access AtmosAI through a modern web browser that supports the
application’s technologies.
- Weather Data Accuracy: AtmosAI relies on information supplied by its external weather
provider. Accuracy is not guaranteed as a result of this.
- Cached Information: When weather data is cached, users are assumed to understand that the
information may not reflect current conditions, but will display accurate information as it
updates periodically.
