3. External Interface Requirements
3.1 User Interfaces
AtmosAI will provide a web-based graphical user interface that allows users to access weather
information and application features through a modern web browser. The interface will have a clear
layout with readable text and straightforward navigation. The main weather screen will display the
selected location, current weather conditions, and access to the forecast and AI-generated daily
summary. Current conditions will include information such as temperature, humidity, wind,
precipitation probability, and a weather description. Users will enter a zip code to search for weather
information and to see a five-day forecast. It will provide adaptable information screen layouts
depending upon the device.
3.2 Hardware Interfaces
AtmosAI is a web-based application intended to operate on desktop computers, laptops,
smartphones, or anything that has a modern web browser. No specialized hardware is required.
Standard input devices such as keyboards and mice will be required for normal user interaction.
Wi-fi connection is required, and secure network communication through HTTPS is needed as
well.
3.3 Software Interfaces
- React and JavaScript: AtmosAI uses React and JavaScript to implement its
web interface and interactive features. These technologies support input,
navigation, and display of weather information, forecasts, maps, and the
AI-generated summaries.
- OpenWeatherMap API: AtmosAI will communicate with the
OpenWeatherMap API to retrieve weather information and forecasts. The
application will process and display the returned data to users. API details are
available at https://openweathermap.org/api.
- OpenAI API: AtmosAI will use the OpenAI API to generate daily weather
summaries and suggested actions. Relevant weather information will be sent to
the service and receive text in response. This functionality depends on valid
API credentials, network connectivity, and the availability of the external
service. API details are available at https://platform.openai.com/docs.
- Web Browser: AtmosAI will operate within a compatible web browser, which
will render the React interface, process user interactions, and support
communication with external services.
- Data Storage: AtmosAI will need to store saved locations, cached information,
and user preferences. Stored information will be used to retrieve saved
locations and display previously retrieved weather data when appropriate.
Software Requirements Specification for AtmosAI Page 8
3.4 Communications Interfaces
- Weather Data Communication: AtmosAI will send requests to the OpenWeatherMap API
containing the location information needed to retrieve weather conditions and forecasts.
This will return weather data in the format specified by the API.
- AI Service Communication: AtmosAI will communicate with the OpenAI API to generate
daily weather summaries and suggested actions. The service will return generated text for
display within the application.
- Communication Security: API credentials must be handled securely and protected from
unauthorized access. Secret API keys won’t be publicly available and will ensure security
for the users.
3.5 Operations
AtmosAI will primarily operate through interactive sessions in a web browser. Users
search for weather information by ZIP code, select saved locations, view forecasts, and
access AI-generated summaries and suggested actions. During normal operation, the
application will retrieve weather information from the OpenWeatherMap API and use
the OpenAI API to generate summaries when requested or as specified. Weather
information may be cached and refreshed every two hours, and the retrieval time will
be displayed for the users. Error messages will be shown if network connectivity errors
occur. Backup and recovery procedures will depend on the application’s data storage
method. Ongoing maintenance is required, and updating API integrations may be
necessary depending on potential API providers.
3.6 Functional Hierarchy
AtmosAI's functionality can be organized into five major groups: weather information, AI weather
assistance, weather visualization and environmental data, location and display preferences, and weather
data management.
1. Weather Information
- Search for weather information by ZIP code.
- View current weather conditions.
- View five-day forecasts.
- View short-term forecasts in 15-minute increments for the next three hours.
2. AI Weather Assistance
- Generate daily weather summaries.
- Provide suggested actions based on available weather information.
3. Weather Visualization and Environmental Data
- Display weather maps.
Software Requirements Specification for AtmosAI Page 9
- View map layers for precipitation, temperature, cloud cover, and wind.
- View Air Quality Index information.
4. Location and Display Preferences
- Save and select up to five locations.
- Change measurement units.
5. Weather Data Management
- Retrieve weather data from the external weather service.
- Cache weather information.
- Display the time weather data was retrieved.
- Refresh cached weather data every two hours.
These functional groups provide a high-level overview of how AtmosAI's capabilities are organized.
Detailed requirements for individual functions are specified in the functional requirements section of
this SRS.
4. System Features
4.1 View Current Weather Conditions (UC-1)
4.1.1 Description and priority
The user will be able to view the current weather conditions such as temperature, wind
speed and direction, and chance of precipitation. This feature is a high priority. This
requirement was derived from user story 2.
4.1.2 Stimulus/Response Sequences
The current weather conditions should load when the user launches the app. The app
will retrieve and display the weather data for the last used zip code.
4.1.3 Functional Requirements
● REQ-1.1: The app shall display weather for the location provided
● REQ-1.2: The app shall display temperature, wind speed and direction, and chance of
precipitation.
● REQ-1.3: The user shall be alerted if weather data can not be accessed due to not
having an internet connection
● REQ-1.4: If the API server does not respond within three attempts, the app will display
an error
4.2 View AI Summary and Suggestion (UC-2)
4.2.1 Description and priority
The user will be able to view an AI generated summary of the day’s weather. The summary
will also include a suggested action, such as bringing an umbrella because it is raining.
This is a high priority. This requirement was derived from ethnography.
4.2.2 Stimulus/Response Sequences
The AI summary should be generated when the user opens the app after the weather
