5. Other Nonfunctional Requirements
5.1 Performance Requirements
The app should not have excessively long load times. Specifically:
● The weather conditions should be displayed within two seconds of the app being launched
● The weather forecast should be displayed within three seconds of the app being launched
● The AI summary should be displayed within ten seconds of the app being launched. This will
provide time for the weather data to be returned and for the server to generate a response.
When reloading due to a new zip code being searched, or the preferred units of measurement being
changed, the features should load in the same times listed above. In cases of weak network connection or
congestion, these times can be increased by five seconds. Cached data should be used when possible to
minimize loading times. This requirement was derived from user stories.
5.2 Safety Requirements
The app must provide accurate weather data. Providing inaccurate weather data could cause users to
prepare incorrectly for potentially dangerous or destructive weather events. To ensure that the app provides
accurate information, the data displayed must be checked to ensure that it matches what is returned from
the weather API. When a user enters a zip code the app must return the correct weather for that area. The
app must clearly display the current location that the weather data is for to help prevent confusion about
what location the user is viewing. This requirement was derived from user stories.
The app must provide up-to-date weather data. Data that is not up-to-date would be inaccurate and have the
same repercussions as providing inaccurate data. The weather data will be updated at least as often as the
Software Requirements Specification for AtmosAI Page 15
API server (every two hours) to ensure that it is up to date. This requirement was derived from user stories.
5.3 Security Requirements
The zip code will be stored securely on the user’s device. It should not be possible to retrieve this data
without physical access to the user’s device. This requirement was derived from ethnography.
5.4 Software Quality Attributes
Correctness is the top priority for this app. As discussed in section 5.2, incorrect weather data can be a safety
risk. Additionally, the AI summary should be tested to ensure that it produces accurate information. The AI
model may need to have restricted access to information to ensure that it produces a correct summary and
does not make something up or use data for another time and/or place. This requirement was derived from
user stories.
Other top priorities are usability, availability, reliability, and portability. The app should be easy to use,
provide the data quickly and consistently when the user has internet access, and the weather app should be
able to run on many different devices. These requirements were derived from ethnography.
5.5 Nonfunctional Requirements Summary
● NFR-1: Performant: load times will be within the restraints set in section 5.1
● NFR-2: Correct: the app will provide data that is accurate and no more than two hours old for the zip
code entered
● NFR-3: Secure: the saved location data will be stored locally. It will be impossible to retrieve this data
remotely
● NFR-4: Usable: even if someone has never used the app before, they should be able to find the
information they are looking for within two minutes
● NFR-5: Available: the features will work as in intended as long as their requirements are met, with an
uptime within 2% of the 95% uptime of the weather API servers
● NFR-6: Reliable: the app will not cause an error when all requirements are met
● NFR-7: Portable: the app can run on mobile devices as well as PCs
